# `tools/shared_sync.py` compares the two repositories byte for byte, so a
# line ending is a difference. A commit made from Windows can land CRLF and
# the check then fails on files whose content is identical -- which is
# exactly what happened to the first sync of the flywheel pages.
#
# LF everywhere, decided here rather than per-machine.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
